  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Paste a human protein sequence and get a phosphorylation probability for every S/T/Y residue, with predicted sites highlighted on the sequence at an adjustable decision threshold. Then pick one site and see which neighbouring residues in a ±15-residue window drove its score, using an occlusion (deletion) test. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
